1820-## Phase 14 — Storyboard and Animator provider migration
1821-
1822:### 14.1 Shared asynchronous media-job service
1823-Build one orchestration layer over the Phase 11 job contract for multi-scene submit, poll/callback,
1824-progress, per-scene results, retry, cancellation, timeout, resume/reconciliation, and terminal
1825-aggregation. It owns managed staging/promotion and execution events; providers own only remote/local
1826-generation mechanics. Adapt the existing Storyboard and Animator job stores/manifests without
1827-changing public job IDs or observable progress behavior.
1828-
1829-**Done when:** deterministic tests cover all-success, partial-success, all-failed, delayed callback,
1830-duplicate callback, restart reconciliation, cancellation, timeout, and retry; all-failed can never be
1831-reported as success; and Storyboard/Animator can share the service without domain-specific branches.
1832-
1833:### 14.2 Storyboard providers behind their interface
1834-Bring `gemini_ws`, `wavespeed_direct`, and `wavespeed_webhook` fully behind `StoryboardProvider` and
1835-Provider Contract v2. Move all provider-ID branching from `studio/storyboard/routes.py`, workflow
1836-adapters, and WebSocket/runtime setup into provider implementations/capabilities. Normalize
1837-storyboard paths, URLs, thumbnails, watermark handling, and per-scene metadata. Repair the audited
1838-legacy-selection gap: bulk `/api/storyboard/generate` currently ignores its accepted `provider` field,
--
1842-**Done when:** routes and `storyboard.generate` resolve/execute providers generically; the three
1843-current IDs/defaults/settings and output artifacts remain compatible; unavailable browser-extension
1844-and invalid-key states are isolated health/errors; and contract tests exercise every provider with
1845-mocked transports.
