## Findings

- **P1 — `ASSET_RESULT` bypasses callback correlation.** [`studio/animator/routes.py:385`](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/animator/routes.py:385) processes URLs without calling `_accept_project`, unlike `ASSET_UPLOAD` and `JOB_COMPLETE`. A stale Grok callback can therefore download files and mark scenes ready in a current Kie job sharing the project ID. Gate the callback before filtering/downloading.

- **P1 — Animator WebSocket uploads are unbounded.** [`studio/animator/routes.py:330`](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/animator/routes.py:330) calculates upload size only for logging, then decodes and writes every image. The equivalent Storyboard handler enforces `MAX_MEDIA_CALLBACK_BYTES`. Large WebSocket payloads can exhaust memory or disk despite Phase 14.4 requiring oversized callbacks to be rejected.

- **P2 — A delayed acknowledgment can discard the wrong pending job.** [`studio/animator/routes.py:95`](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/animator/routes.py:95) handles any `JOB_RECEIVED` with `hub.drop_pending()` rather than `hub.drop_pending(pid)`. If job B replaces job A in the single-slot queue before A’s acknowledgment arrives, A’s delayed acknowledgment clears B, preventing B from being replayed after reconnect. `JOB_COMPLETE` has the same ordering problem at line 108.

- **P2 — Workflow cancellation leaves Grok work queued.** [`studio/animator/providers/grok_automa/provider.py:75`](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/animator/providers/grok_automa/provider.py:75) retains every submission for late delivery, but the provider inherits the no-op [`cancel_job`](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/animator/providers/base.py:66). Consequently, a canceled workflow can later generate assets when the extension reconnects. Cancellation should remove that project’s pending message and terminalize its manifest. Kie similarly records an in-flight result without rechecking cancellation after the remote call.

- **P2 — Grok quality is omitted from the immediate WebSocket dispatch.** [`studio/animator/providers/grok_automa/provider.py:75`](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/animator/providers/grok_automa/provider.py:75) sends mode, duration, and auto-type but not the computed `quality`. The extension can auto-start from this message before its HTTP pending poll refreshes `grok_quality`, silently using the previous/default quality. Existing tests assert quality only in `grabber_job.json`, not in the dispatched message.

Verification: `pytest -q tests` passed with **889 passed, 10 skipped, 328 subtests**. The findings are coverage gaps rather than existing test failures.
